      </CheatEntries>
    </CheatEntry>
  </CheatEntries>
  <UserdefinedSymbols/>
  <Comments>Actraiser Renaissance (Steam/PC)
Includes separate script groups for Act Mode / side-scroller gameplay and Settlement / Angel Mode.

Act Mode Infinite HP captures the exact live player parameter-block pointer during ActlReadObject.CallFixedUpdate, then filters the authoritative shared SVObjParamater.Damage routine by pointer identity. Infinite MP resolves SceneAct.playerReader and continuously copies the live maximum ExpUniValues float into both the current MP value object and display cache. Infinite Lives keeps SaveData.actContinueCnt (continues used) at zero; zero corresponds to the displayed three lives. Super Damage multiplies the final positive damage calculated by ActlReadObject.CallGetDamage for every parameter block except the exact live player block by ten. One-Hit Kill substitutes the target's exact current HP at the adjacent final-damage write. No Player Hit Detection exits ActlReadObject.CallGetDamage only when its target owns the exact live player parameter block, preventing the game's damage reaction and knockback processing while leaving enemy targets and the player's attack path unchanged. It fails open whenever the player identity chain is unavailable and is compatible with the other Act Mode scripts. Teleport to Nearest Gold Scroll uses Cheat Engine's native table-hotkey system and activates directly with J; the row does not need to remain checked. Each press searches only the current ACTOL object registry for the live act_gmk_ITEMSTATUE_GOLD collectible family, chooses the nearest target by real XY distance, invokes the game's own SVObject.Teleport routine so its Rigidbody2D, transform, velocity, camera, and ACTOL cache remain synchronized, and automatically resets the entry for the next press. The row records SUCCESS or the exact last error. If the current loaded section has no live gold scroll statue or the lookup fails, it leaves the player untouched and plays Cheat Engine's short error beep without a popup.

Settlement / Angel Mode Infinite HP and Infinite SP hook the angel-specific CRTAngel setters and replace attempted changes with the live maxHp or maxSp field. Angel SP Value = 90 keeps both the saved value and visible HUD counter at 90 while enabled and restores its previous saved value when disabled. It is compatible with Infinite Angel SP.

Death Aura - Cave Monsters Only targets CRTMonsterBase.CheckHit, which is shared by the ordinary cave-spawned settlement monsters but not the separate CRTTDMonster invasion/siege system. It queues each roaming monster's exact remaining HP through the native hit pipeline so the game retains its normal death animation, rewards, counters, and cleanup. It does not damage caves/nests, buildings, the angel, or siege attackers.

Max Realm Resources keeps the active realm's material/resource counter at 999 and synchronizes its HUD display. Infinite Usable Items prevents negative ItemManager quantity changes for normal inventory IDs while preserving pickups and the separate realm-resource ID. Fort Build Limit &amp; Fence Capacity = 99 raises the permanent-fort construction cap and normal-fence carrying capacity, along with their HUD maximums, without changing placement rules or material costs. Fence Stock = 99 separately keeps both the active realm inventory and the temporary raid inventory of normal fences at 99 and synchronizes the HUD; it deliberately leaves the special decoy/bell fence's scripted use count unchanged. Invincible Forts &amp; Fences blocks CRTFort.SetDamage before HP loss or damaging conditions are applied; monsters and the temple use separate routines.

Super Champions targets only the six objects exposed by CRTHeroManager. While enabled, HP, Attack, Defense, Magic Defense, Fire Resistance, and Ice Resistance are set to 999; champion damage is blocked; normal and special attack range/arc are greatly expanded; and attack cooldown is reduced to 0.15 seconds. It updates both the live combat block and the runtime datatable copy used by Ally Profiles and newly spawned champions. Original values are restored on disable, and no boosted values are written into saved level/progression data.

No Miracle Cooldowns makes new cooldown durations zero and clears the live normal/special cooldown arrays. Super Forts targets only the gate/defense and arrow/magic fort lists, setting Attack, Defense, Magic Defense, and elemental resistances to 999, reducing attack cooldown to 0.15 seconds, expanding attack/projectile range to 20, and raising simultaneous targets to 20; fences are excluded. All Legendary Chronicles = 999 targets the six documented experience-book item IDs 25-30. Instant Champion Summon continuously refills the summon gauge through its native update and availability routines without bypassing champion unlock eligibility or forcing duplicate/already-active champions.

Safe Game Speed uses Cheat Engine's speed control at a conservative 2x and restores normal 1x speed when disabled.

Settlement combat scripts remain isolated from Act Mode and enemy health. The Act damage entries resolve SceneAct.playerReader.gameParamater and leave that exact player pointer on the unmodified path; this avoids the unused zero-valued ParamType fields found on live enemies.

Attach Cheat Engine to ActraiserR.exe, expand the group, and activate entries individually.</Comments>
</CheatTable>
